      "id": "0037-default-keeps-a-present-empty-string",
      "title": "default keeps a present empty string",
      "since": "0.35.0",
      "tags": [
        "template",
        "filters"
      ],
      "fn": "render",
      "input": {
        "template": {
          "fancyTemplate": 1,
          "writer": "fine-print",
          "variables": {
            "v": {
              "type": "string"
            }
          },
          "document": {
            "blocks": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "runs": [
                  {
                    "text": "[{{ v | default:\"N/A\" }}]"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "data": {
          "v": ""
        }
      },
      "expected": {
        "ok": true,
        "document": {
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "runs": [
                {
                  "text": "[]"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "notes": "Present and empty is not absent (SPEC 7: the input unchanged if present). A `default` that also replaced \"\" would quietly turn a deliberate blank into placeholder text. Added after fancy-template's sabotage pass found that no row pinned it: treating \"\" as absent left every other row green."
    }
